{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere","title":"cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.md","line":764,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex#cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","label":"cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere","line":1648,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[quarter-pinched sphere theorem]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere}\n\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0280}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem, thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity}\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.5.6}\n  Let $M$ be a closed simply connected $n$-manifold with $4>\\sec\\ge1$. Then\n  $M$ is $(n-1)$-connected, hence a homotopy sphere.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem, thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity}\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity}, \\(\\operatorname{inj}>\\pi/2\\); then \\cref{thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem} gives \\((n-1)\\)-connectivity and a homotopy sphere.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[quarter-pinched sphere theorem] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d6368362d72617563682d6265726765722d6b6c696e67656e626572672d737068657265\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0280</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:6.5.6</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a closed simply connected <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$4&gt;\\sec \\ge 1$\">$4&gt;\\sec \\ge 1$</span>. Then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(n-1)$\">$(n-1)$</span>-connected, hence a homotopy sphere.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity\">↗ thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity</a> \\sketch By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d6b6c696e67656e626572672d70696e6368696e672d696e6a6563746976697479\">section 5</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {inj}&gt;\\pi /2$\">$\\operatorname {inj}&gt;\\pi /2$</span>; then <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI%23thm%3Apet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368362d6265726765722d7370686572652d7468656f72656d\">section 5</a> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(n-1)$\">$(n-1)$</span>-connectivity and a homotopy sphere. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-ricci-simply-connected","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity","title":"thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity","label":"thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity"}],"backlinks":[],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere","title":"cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere","tex":"\\begin{corollary}[quarter-pinched sphere theorem]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch6-rauch-berger-klingenberg-sphere}\n\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0280}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem, thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity}\n  \\dcref{ch6:6.5.6}\n  Let $M$ be a closed simply connected $n$-manifold with $4>\\sec\\ge1$. Then\n  $M$ is $(n-1)$-connected, hence a homotopy sphere.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem, thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity}\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity}, \\(\\operatorname{inj}>\\pi/2\\); then \\cref{thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem} gives \\((n-1)\\)-connectivity and a homotopy sphere.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch6-berger-sphere-theorem","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_SectionalCurvatureComparisonI#thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity","title":"thm:pet-ch6-klingenberg-pinching-injectivity","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}